<BaseLayout
  title="About :: Jesse Wunderlich"
  description="Who Jesse Wunderlich is — Marine, drone operator, serial builder, husband and dad in Frazee, Minnesota."
  ogTitle="About Jesse Wunderlich">
  <div class="box">
    <h2>&gt; about_me.txt</h2>
    <p>I grew up the oldest of seven kids, moving constantly while my dad was alive — always the
    new kid, never anywhere long enough to build much of a social life. That made me
    self-reliant and a little introverted, more comfortable building things than working a room.</p>
    <p>The Marine Corps gave me structure and belonging. I served as a Sergeant from 2013 to 2018,
    boot camp at MCRD San Diego. After I got out I jumped straight into contracting, and these days
    I fly the ScanEagle as a UAS operator — which means a lot of months overseas every year.</p>
    <p>I've tracked my net worth since high school; being disciplined with money is something
    Charlotte and I have always shared. I married my best friend in 2021, and we're raising our
    crew up here in the Minnesota lakes with three rescued Cane Corsos underfoot.</p>
    <p>The long game: build <a href="/projects/">Nova</a> into something self-sufficient so I can
    trade the deployments for being home with my kids.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="box">
    <h2>&gt; vitals</h2>
    <ul class="now">
      <li>📍 Frazee, MN (originally Fargo, ND)</li>
      <li>🦅 USMC Sgt (ret) · Service-Disabled Veteran</li>
      <li>🛩️ Drone operator by day, builder by night</li>
      <li>🧠 INTJ · introvert · serial entrepreneur</li>
      <li>☕ Doesn't drink coffee (yes, really)</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
